ngterm: Kitty placement-id namespaces and relative placements' parent links in the C API (interim, retired by the
render-state image API adoption)

The storage placement iterator at LIBGHOSTTY_VT_REV (v1.4.0) still reports a placement's id without its namespace
and a relative placement (P=/Q=) without its parent, so an embedder cannot draw what Ghostty's renderer draws:
placeholderTarget looks a named id up among the client's (external) ids only and, with none named, prefers a client's
virtual placement (PlacementId.preferredOver); src/renderer/image.zig positions a relative placement whose chain
roots at a virtual placement at the root's minimum placeholder cell plus the chain's summed offsets
(pending_relative). This patch only reads out what storage holds, additively, with no logic of its own
(the embedder resolves chains, targets and positions):

- GHOSTTY_KITTY_GRAPHICS_PLACEMENT_DATA_PLACEMENT_ID_NAMESPACE (GhosttyKittyPlacementIdNamespace: INTERNAL for a
  terminal-numbered id, EXTERNAL for the client's p=), the placement key's tag;
- GHOSTTY_KITTY_GRAPHICS_PLACEMENT_DATA_PARENT_IMAGE_ID, _PARENT_PLACEMENT_ID, _PARENT_PLACEMENT_ID_NAMESPACE,
  _RELATIVE_HORIZONTAL_OFFSET and _RELATIVE_VERTICAL_OFFSET: the fields of a relative placement's location
  (Placement.Relative: the parent's key and H=/V=), GHOSTTY_NO_VALUE for a placement that is not relative;
- the enum in the ABI type manifest (types.zig), and tests.

v1.4.0's render-state image API (#14780, #14789) resolves placeholders and relative chains inside the library; once
the wrapper and renderer draw from it, this patch goes. Until then it is rebased as is: v1.4.0 reworked the header
around an unchanged GhosttyKittyGraphicsPlacementData (1..12), so the enum hunk now sits after its Z member and the
test hunk at the file's new end.

Nothing existing changes. Applied by scripts/build-ghostty-vt.sh; the bindings are regenerated with
scripts/gen-ghostty-vt-bindings.sh.

